-		<English>[H1]World Advisor Territory Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Territory tab counts plots and map assets owned by the selected player. It separates plots inside city big fat crosses from the rest of the player's owned land so empire-wide resources can be read without losing city-workable context.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]BFC: owned plots that are inside at least one selected-player city's big fat cross.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Sub: suburbs; owned plots outside all selected-player city big fat crosses. These plots are controlled territory, but no selected-player city can work them directly unless a city is founded, captured or culturally expanded differently later.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Tot: total owned plots or assets, equal to BFC plus Sub.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The World Advisor respects normal map knowledge: hidden or unexplored plots and bonuses stay hidden unless debug mode is active. More entries can therefore appear as territory and city BFCs become fully explored, or when debug mode lets you inspect another player.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Hover over a row icon for the usual tooltip, or click it to open the corresponding Sevopedia entry when one exists.</English>
+		<English>[H1]World Advisor Territory Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Territory tab counts plots and map assets owned by the selected player. It separates plots inside city big fat crosses from the rest of the player's owned land so empire-wide resources can be read without losing city-workable context.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]BFC: owned plots that are inside at least one selected-player city's big fat cross.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Sub: suburbs; owned plots outside all selected-player city big fat crosses. These plots are controlled territory, but no selected-player city can work them directly unless a city is founded, captured or culturally expanded differently later.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Tot: total owned plots or assets, equal to BFC plus Sub.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Some plot rows overlap because they describe different properties of the same plots. For example, a Peak is also Land, and a riverside Grassland is both River and Grassland. Therefore the Plots table's Total row is a real plot count, not the sum of every visible row.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The World Advisor respects normal map knowledge: hidden or unexplored plots and bonuses stay hidden unless debug mode is active. More entries can therefore appear as territory and city BFCs become fully explored, or when debug mode lets you inspect another player.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Hover over a row icon for the usual tooltip, or click it to open the corresponding Sevopedia entry when one exists.</English>
 	</TEXT>

