 - Reworked the **Military Advisor** in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now with Unit Combat and Units **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5530+) Note: **icon size** is **increased** at **higher resolutions** (e.g., from 24 to 32 if resolution height >= 1440). Note 2: as of now the [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) is not supported.
 - Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5519+) Players can **optionally** set an **alternative lower right space for scoreboard** on **lower game resolutions** (e.g., 1920*1080) so that an **extra column or more is visible** in the technology advisor, and an **alternative top space space** for **advisor buttons** (in map view) because this alternative right space may cover these advisor buttons. **Boldened title** for consistency. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5520+) See also [KI#114](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#114---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-tech-advisor-on-save-load-initially-shown-current-tech-missing-turns-left-timer-until-another-tech-is-clicked). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5691+) **When opening** Technology Advisor, **right-align scoreboard leader text** so it is easier to read (because text is often not visible due to advisor width expansion). **On Technology Advisor close**, it **reverts back** to usual alignment.
 - **Inverted BUG Options** for the **Technology Advisor** and the **Religion Advisor** so they are more accessible. They are now **enabled as a default**, and ticking their box disables them. Rewrote their text for clarity (e.g. "GP Research" -> **"Hide bulbing indicators"**). See [Inverted BUG options](/README.md#inverted-bug-options).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **World Advisor**: shows **detailed BFC, suburbs, and territory geography** information as **sortable tables**. BFC tabs show information **per city (rows)** and **per field (columns)**, and have a **click to enter city button** (similar to the Info Screen's Wonders tab). The BFC1 tab shows mostly **plot type** and **terrains/features** information; the BFC2 tab shows mostly **bonuses** and **improvements** information. The Territory tab shows a **condensed summary** with 4 tables of the former BFC tabs, with a BFC, suburbs (i.e. plots outside BFC) and **Total counts (columns)** for each field (rows), with **hover support** and **pedia redirect on click** (if a corresponding pedia page exists), and a legend link. The **environment tab** is now part of the World advisor (better thematic fit).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5718+) New **World Advisor**: shows **detailed BFC, suburbs, and territory geography** information as **sortable tables**. BFC tabs show **counts per city (rows) and per field (columns)**, and have a **click to enter city button** (similar to the Info Screen's Wonders tab). The BFC1 tab shows mostly **plot type** (Peak, Hill, Water, Land) and other information (**River, Lake, Coastal Land, sortable City found year and population**) and **Terrains/Features** information; the BFC2 tab shows mostly **Bonuses** and **Improvements** with other information (**Routes**). The Territory tab shows a **condensed summary** with 4 tables of the former BFC tabs, with a BFC, suburbs (i.e. plots outside BFC) and **Total counts (columns)** for each field (rows), with **hover support** and **pedia redirect on click** (if a corresponding pedia page exists), and a legend link. Note: totals are not the strict sum of all rows as some may overlap (e.g., river and hill can be on same plot). The **environment tab** is now part of the World advisor (better thematic fit).
 - Did a similar rework of the **Info Screen** in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py); in particular in **Top 5 Cities** we now use a multilist to display more wonders in a prettier way, and in the **Wonders** tab we now **show the Wonders' Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the first column (**click to move to city** mechanic is moved to the City column instead); the **Statistics** tab now also shows buttons (plus **change default ordering** from alphabetical to **from most to least Built** (avoids tedious manual user ordering each time)), and the **Graph** Tab and possibly other tabs also show buttons (e.g., **leader icons before text**, **emojis**). Also added other information (e.g., turn numbers in the Graph tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5718+) **Removed** the **Improvements table** from the Statistics tab, because it was **inconsistent** with how Units and Buidings show all-time total **built**, Improvements would only show **current** possession (e.g., building a farm, replacing it with a cottage, then replacing it again with a farm would be Current 1 farm, not total built 2 farms), plus the World Advisor is a **better thematic fit**.
 - Additionally, added in the **Info Screen** a new **Timeline Tab**, showing a **text-colored spoiler-free** account of the key moments that happened each turn. Based on the **ReplayScreen**'s text, so **preserves information on save reload** unlike the Event Log. Optional **LOG button** allows to export to `PythonDbg.log` text file the output, and has optional **caching** for performance. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: Timeline Tab](/README.md#timeline-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
 - Added in the **Info Screen** a new **Score Tab** showing a **sortable (default ordered by highest score) table** with all relevant scoreboard fields, plus **new fields** like Player color, Player ID (to distinguish identical Name/Civ/Leader/Player Color), (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5532+) Traits (T1 and T2) as **icon chars**, total Power (of a player, distinct from power ratios), total Power per City, Land%, V/M, Tech (total techs). Added a clickable **"Legend"** text that **redirects to Sevopedia Concepts' "Score Tab Columns" page**. Note that unlike military ratios, PowT and PoT/C are shown even for the human player, since these vary every turn. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: Score Tab](/README.md#score-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).

